{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall be if they do not believe.</b> For is there any doubt before the Holy One, blessed be He? And further, had He not already said ״וְשָׁמְעוּ לְקוֹלֶךָ״? Perhaps, however, the measure of the matter is thus: וְהָיָה אִם — if you still feel further concern, and this sign will not suffice for you to say that through it they will surely believe." "It further appears that He intended to tell him to remove also a doubt that is not visible, namely, that perhaps Israel will not settle the faith firmly in their hearts, even though outwardly no lack of faith would be recognized. Therefore He said ״אִם לֹא יַאֲמִינוּ״ etc. And this doubt Moses could not possibly clarify, to say of it who is uncertain before Heaven by saying ״אִם לֹא״ — for these are matters of the heart. And the Master came to remove from him the doubt of a weakening of faith in Israel's heart through the medium of the three signs." "<b>And the waters etc.</b> The light of Israel's eyes, Rashi z״l, it appears in his view that the reason for His saying ״וְהָיוּ וְהָיוּ״ is to say that they would not become blood until they were on the dry land. Words of holy grace. And I add in it a reason for praise: it is because of the Master's own command that Aaron would strike with his staff at the Nile, and they said z״l (Exodus Rabbah 9:10) that Moses could not strike the Nile because it protected him. And here HaShem commanded that he take from the waters of the Nile and they would become blood, and it was contrived that the blow would not come through Moses. Therefore He said <b>וְהָיוּ</b> — they would be, in their continued state, as long as they were in his hand; only after they were on the dry land would they become blood. And through this, their affliction would not come through Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:24.207998469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}